  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\r\n\r\n## Repro steps\r\n\r\n1. Open a webpage which has an input or a textarea element similar to the following HTML.\r\n```html  \r\n<body>\r\n    <main>\r\n    youhoo\r\n    <textarea>coucou</textarea>\r\n    <input value=\"inputValue\" />\r\n    </main>\r\n </body>\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Change values of the input box by focusing the element and typing text\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93727321-9e5c-4aaf-ac9d-d853a7358ddb)\r\n\r\n3. Select all elements on the page using Ctrl/Cmd + A.\r\n\r\n4. Open a new Gmail compose email page and paste.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac6a2b30-45f8-41e5-a6dd-0556c9a55d91)\r\n\r\n### Expectation\r\nThe pasted HTML content should reflect the latest changes made by the user on the input/textarea elements.\r\n\r\n### Actual\r\nThe pasted HTML only has the initial values of the input and not the changed values.\r\nHowever, on pasting as plain text, latest input values are reflected as expected.\r\n\r\nThis is true for both Firefox and Chromium today. \r\n\r\n## Additional comments\r\nIdeally, when copying selection and pasting as HTML, the user should to see the same content as visible on the web page.\r\n",
